			"text": "Shuleichthys is a ray-finned fish discovered in Gansu Province of China, dating back to the Early Cretaceous. Its name is a mix of 'Shule' the name of a river going through the Changma Basin and 'Ichthys' meaning fish. Their size ranged from 6 centimeters to 18 centimeters in size, with a relatively small anal fin compared to other stem osteoglossomorphs."
